      "lead": "Monitoring and control of LoRaWAN sensors and actuators, published by Object as a Service. I built the Angular front end and improved the Django back end.",
      "periodLabel": "2023 — 2026",
      "client": "Object as a Service",
      "role": "Full-stack web developer",
      "place": "Remote",
      "siteUrl": "https://iotplatform.fr/fr/",
      "techs": [
        "angular",
        "ngrx",
        "django"
      ],
      "featured": false,
      "article": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Context"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "IOTPlatform lets industrial operators, network managers and local authorities monitor and control their equipment remotely: level, flow or temperature sensors, and actuators, on the Orange LoRa and The Things Network networks."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The platform collects and decodes the frames sent by devices, triggers alerts by email or SMS, and sends commands to actuators."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What I did"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I owned the whole Angular front end: designing pages and components, API calls and state management with NgRx."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "On the Django back end, I improved the existing code and added several features."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "bulletList",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Monitoring dashboards across several sites."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Sending commands to actuators, with their history."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Configuring email and SMS alerts."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "listItem",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Time-series charts and CSV data export."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Technical choices"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Data comes from many devices and changes often. I centralised application state with NgRx: screens read the same store, API calls go through effects, and updated data is updated everywhere at once."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "I split the interface into reusable components (tables, charts, forms) shared between screens. The interface stays consistent as features are added."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Outcome"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The Angular front end is the clients' entry point for monitoring, commands and alerts."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 2
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What I learned"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Working on a live product taught me to evolve existing code without breaking what clients use every day."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "NgRx takes more code up front, but it keeps application behaviour predictable as screens multiply."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
